comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for subscriptions/listen resourceSubscriptions Streamable HTTP Mcp-Session-Id Last-Event-ID Mcp-Method Mcp-Name x-mcp-header and stream retry. No item covers the new transport model."
  "2026-08-25T19:16:13.729Z","harness:codex","Execution scope: SDK-owned subscription contracts, stdio dispatch, Streamable HTTP header validation, request-scoped notification isolation, retry/disconnect semantics, tests, docs, and release evidence."
  "2026-08-25T19:54:19.554Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added SDK-owned subscription filtering/correlation and schema-derived HTTP headers, real sessionless pm-mcp-http POST/SSE transport, stdio parity, asynchronous sink backpressure, response-stream disconnect cleanup, fresh-id retry proof, additive SDK snapshot, and operator docs. Focused transport/stateless tests are green."
  "2026-08-25T21:13:12.496Z","harness:codex","Evidence: shipped public subscription and transport SDK contracts, stdio and Streamable HTTP adapters, schema-derived headers, backpressure/cancel/close semantics, package bin, documentation, and compatibility tests. Exact repository verification passed 581 files / 7,982 tests with 100% statements (58,983/58,983), branches (44,433/44,433), functions (12,277/12,277), and lines (56,823/56,823). Linked run test-local-mt95vmrt-9rnex3 passed all 3 commands, including package artifact, npx smoke, and 88-command package-first dogfood. An installed-package HTTP-bin smoke caught the npm symlink realpath entrypoint defect; the shared realpath-aware main-module guard fixed it, and a fresh packed install successfully imported the SDK and served server/discover over the published pm-mcp-http bin."
  "2026-08-25T21:56:23.388Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: linked run completed all three commands against the final concurrency-hardened code: 57 focused MCP tests, packed artifact plus npx consumer smoke, and 88-command package-first dogfood. A fresh npm install of the packed tarball imported the public SDK at protocol 2026-07-28 and launched node_modules/.bin/pm-mcp-http through the real npm symlink; server/discover returned HTTP 200 with supportedVersions [2026-07-28]. The exact repository run passed 581 files / 7,986 tests with 100% statements (59,009/59,009), branches (44,444/44,444), functions (12,283/12,283), and lines (56,846/56,846)."
  "2026-08-25T22:27:15.163Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head remediation evidence: DeepScan flagged the integration helper's id === undefined branch as unreachable because its default parameter narrowed undefined away; the helper now models valid JSON-RPC request ids as string | number | null and emits id directly, with the existing notification tests continuing to remove id explicitly. Gates (static) independently flagged collectMcpHeaderAnnotations at CodeFactor complexity 18 over the repository ceiling 16; annotation validation is now isolated in a documented parser and the exact static gate reports zero violations. Verification after both review-caught fixes: affected suites 18/18, TypeScript contracts pass, repository coverage 581/581 files and 7,986/7,986 tests at exact 100% (59,013 statements, 44,446 branches, 12,284 functions, 56,848 lines), and CODEFACTOR_BASE_REF=origin/main pnpm lint passes through the complete static assurance chain."
  "2026-08-25T22:57:38.850Z","harness:codex","Hosted-review remediation evidence (final code before close): addressed subscription/transport findings by delaying SSE headers until registry/filter validation, serializing sink writes with a bounded 5s write deadline, decoupling tool-call responses from notification backpressure, suppressing undefined result payloads, rejecting malformed non-string methods, and adding direct-subscription/stdio/HTTP close-race and stale-registry coverage. Exact local proof: node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 581 files / 7,990 tests with 59,056/59,056 statements, 44,456/44,456 branches, 12,296/12,296 functions, and 56,887/56,887 lines; CODEFACTOR_BASE_REF=origin/main pnpm lint exited 0, including ESLint, jscpd, static complexity, SDK surface/import-cost, MCP inventory, tracker quality, and record-integrity gates."
  "2026-08-25T23:00:41.068Z","harness:codex","Final linked-test execution after hosted-review remediation: all 3 linked commands passed — 37 focused subscription/transport/HTTP tests, package-artifact plus packed-npx smoke, and package-first dogfood (88 commands). No linked test was skipped."
  "2026-08-26T00:03:44.331Z","harness:codex","Second exact-head review remediation evidence: corrected the governed streaming-model body to state that the subscriptions/listen JSON-RPC request id is the subscription id, matching the official 2026-07-28 schema. Closed the HTTP open-time disconnect race by registering cleanup before acknowledgment, handling already-destroyed/ended responses, and making SSE drain/close listener attachment race-free. Negative controls cover close events and destroyed/writable-ended states during acknowledgment, synchronous close, and synchronous write failure. Literal-final proof: 581 files / 7,992 tests, exact 100% coverage (59,126 statements; 44,508 branches; 12,301 functions; 56,953 lines); full non-interactive lint/static assurance exited 0; all 3 linked commands passed, including 38 focused transport tests, package/npx smoke, and 88-command dogfood."
