close_reason: "Delivered and review-hardened MCP subscriptions and transports with schema-correct JSON-RPC subscription identity, race-free HTTP disconnect cleanup, exact coverage, static assurance, package smoke, and dogfood proof."
body: "## Streaming model\n\n- subscriptions/listen is one long-lived POST-response stream whose JSON-RPC request id is the subscription identifier stamped on every delivered notification.\n- tools, prompts, resources, and resource-subscription changes flow only through the opted-in listen stream.\n- progress and message notifications remain on the response stream of their originating request.\n- A broken request stream loses that in-flight request and the client retries with a new JSON-RPC request id.\n- STDIO and Streamable HTTP share SDK handlers, cancellation, ordering, backpressure, heartbeat policy, and structured failures.\n- Streamable HTTP validates Mcp-Method and Mcp-Name and supports declared x-mcp-header parameter mappings without header injection."
